<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Karamanli Tripoli</h1><p class="st-meta">1711 CE – 1835 CE · capital Tripoli</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The hereditary Karamanli pashas of Tripoli, a corsair dynasty best known for fighting the United States in the First Barbary War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1711 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-karamanli">Ahmed Karamanli</a>, a cavalry officer of mixed Turkish and local descent, seized power in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-tripoli">Tripoli</a>, massacred his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">Janissary</a> rivals and founded a dynasty. The Ottoman sultan recognised him as pasha, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ottoman-tripolitania">Ottoman Tripolitania</a> became a hereditary, largely autonomous state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Karamanli pashas lived from corsairing, tribute from European powers and the trans-Saharan trade through the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-fezzan">Fezzan</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-karamanli">Yusuf Karamanli</a> annexed in 1812. Yusuf, who ruled from 1795, declared war on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> in 1801; the frigate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a> was captured, and American forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derna">Derna</a> in 1805 before a peace treaty.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After European pressure ended corsairing and tribute, debts mounted and civil war broke out in 1832. In 1835 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> sent a fleet, deposed the last Karamanli and restored direct rule as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tripolitania-vilayet">Tripolitania Vilayet</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/karamanli-tripoli.jpg" alt="Karamanli Tripoli" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Orwellianist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Ottoman_Empire_(1844%E2%80%931922).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1711 CE – 1835 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tripoli</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ahmed Karamanli, Ali Karamanli, Yusuf Karamanli</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Ottoman Turkish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Karamanli dynasty, Regency of Tripoli (Karamanli), Pashalik of Tripoli</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1773&amp;focus=karamanli-tripoli" aria-label="Karamanli Tripoli on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5018 983 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Karamanli Tripoli lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5338 1239L5368 1481M5338 1239L5338 1239M5338 1239L5709 970M5338 1239L5338 1239"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5368 1481h0M5338 1239h0M5709 970h0M5338 1239h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5338 1239h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5338 1239h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tripoli. <a href="/atlas?year=1773&amp;focus=karamanli-tripoli">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
